Date: 16-FEB-1987 13:58:40
From: SYSKERMIT%vax1.central.lancaster.ac.uk@CS.UCL.AC.UK
Subject: Updated C86PRO.A86
Keywords: C86 Kermit

  This is an update to C86PRO.A86, by Chris Lock of Nottingham University. It
makes the C86 Kermit resilient to packets being echoed back to it. Chris did it
orginally for a specific implementation talking to a specific weird British
mainframe, but this part of his code should be of general use in all the C86
implementations. 

            Alan

